at didn't\nDiscoverability of past issues was weak. Several readers wrote in asking for an earlier recipe, and their feedback was mostly positive but pointed out that the archive link was hard to find on the intranet. Right now it sits in the page footer, under two other menus. We also saw mobile rendering issues in two issues, where cards stacked out of order in one email client. The optional reader survey got a 12% response rate, which is lower than we'd like for drawing conclusions about individual sections.\n\n5. Recommendations for Q2\n- Keep the card layout as the default for the weekly wellbeing newsletter and retire the long-form template.\n- Move the archive link into the newsletter header and add a matching link on the intranet landing page.\n- Try a Friday send time for four issues and compare open and click rates against the current Tuesday send.\n- We should expand the pilot to the monthly events digest next, since two team admins have asked for the same format.\n\n— end —\n"} status=200 text_chars=2874 user_message_index=1
